## Sector Analysis — External Energy Flows

Sectors map **energies arriving from outside the system** that cannot be controlled, only managed.

| Sector | What to map | Design response |
|--------|-------------|-----------------|
| **Solar** | Summer/winter sun arcs, shading angles | Orient paths, glass houses, thermal mass |
| **Wind** | Prevailing wind direction, cold blasts, sea breezes | Windbreaks, shelterbelts, living fences |
| **Water** | Surface runoff paths, flood risk, fog collection zones | Swales, retention ponds, diversion drains |
| **Fire** | Fire approach vectors, dry grass corridors | Firebreaks, stone zones, moist plantings |
| **Views** | Valued landscape views, privacy needs | Frame or screen strategically |
| **Noise** | Road, industrial, neighbor noise | Dense planting buffers |
| **Frost** | Cold air drainage paths, frost pockets | Avoid planting frost-sensitive species in drainage hollows |
| **Wildlife** | Beneficial predators vs. pest corridors | Habitat stacking, exclusion zones |

