## Guild Design — Plant Community Vocabulary

A **guild** is a community of plants, animals, insects, and fungi that cooperate to support a central element (usually a fruit or nut tree).

### Classic Fruit Tree Guild Components
| Layer | Function | Example species |
|-------|----------|-----------------|
| Central tree | Yield + canopy | Apple, Pear, Mango, Avocado |
| Nitrogen fixers | Fertility | Comfrey (dynamic), Alder (nodule) |
| Pest confusers | Protection | Chives, Garlic, Marigold |
| Pollinator attractors | Reproduction | Borage, Phacelia, Sweet cicely |
| Ground cover | Mulch + soil | White clover, Creeping thyme |
| Mulch/Chop-and-drop | Biomass | Comfrey, Yarrow, Lemon balm |
| Insectary plants | Beneficial habitat | Dill, Fennel, Buckwheat |
| Bulb layer | Pest deterrence | Daffodil (mole repellent), Alliums |

